OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G1/15
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSCStormont backs call for BBC       
OL,4,CNorthern Ireland to explain cuts       
OL,6,FThe Northern Ireland Assembly has      
OL,7,Fbacked an SDLP motion calling on BBC   
OL,8,FNorthern Ireland to explain its cuts to
OL,9,Fprogrammes and services, after a debate
OL,10,Fon Monday in which MLAs from across the
OL,11,Fchamber criticised the broadcaster.    
OL,13,FThe motion was agreed without a vote.  
OL,14,FIt expresses concern at "sudden cuts to
OL,15,Fmuch loved and vital services",        
OL,16,Fincluding Irish language services and  
OL,17,Flong-running local series, made without
OL,18,F"a clear and publicly explained        
OL,19,Fstrategy".                             
OL,23,EPub: 16-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,143,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14202
SC,0002
PS,C000
CT,5,T
OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 142 Tue 17 NovC16:41/43
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G2/15
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSCStormont backs call for BBC       
OL,4,CNorthern Ireland to explain cuts       
OL,6,FIt calls on BBC NI to explain how it   
OL,7,Fallocates and prioritises resources,   
OL,8,Famid public concern about editorial    
OL,9,Faccountability.                        
OL,11,FOpening the debate, Opposition Leader  
OL,12,FMatthew O'Toole said public service    
OL,13,Fmedia mattered more than ever "at a    
OL,14,Ftime when billionaires or even         
OL,15,Ftrillionaires" were buying social media
OL,16,Fplatforms and using them as weapons. He
OL,17,Fsaid the SDLP supported a licence      
OL,18,Ffee-funded BBC.                        
OL,23,EPub: 16-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,143,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14203
SC,0003
PS,C000
CT,5,T
OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 142 Tue 17 NovC16:41/43
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G3/15
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSCStormont backs call for BBC       
OL,4,CNorthern Ireland to explain cuts       
OL,6,FHe described the decision to make 60%  
OL,7,Fof BBC NI's in-house Irish language    
OL,8,Fstaff redundant as "remarkable". He    
OL,9,Fsaid the BBC's claim that this would   
OL,10,Fnot reduce the service was "simply     
OL,11,Fimplausible".                          
OL,13,FHe also criticised the closure of the  
OL,14,Ffactual programming department, the    
OL,15,Faxing of Give My Head Peace and A      
OL,16,FPerforated Ulster "via e-mail", and the
OL,17,F"slow unwinding" of Radio Foyle.       
OL,23,EPub: 16-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,143,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14204
SC,0004
PS,C000
CT,5,T
OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 142 Tue 17 NovC16:41/43
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G4/15
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSCStormont backs call for BBC       
OL,4,CNorthern Ireland to explain cuts       
OL,6,FO'Toole also turned to UTV. In his     
OL,7,Fclosing speech he said UTV was         
OL,8,F"effectively shutting down its factual 
OL,9,Fprogramme-making", and warned of "a    
OL,10,Fpotential crisis emerging in our       
OL,11,Ftraditional broadcasters here".        
OL,13,FHe contrasted BBC NI with BBC          
OL,14,FDirector-General Matt Brittin, who has 
OL,15,Fappeared before a Commons committee,   
OL,16,Fand RTE Director-General Kevin         
OL,17,FBakhurst, a regular at Oireachtas      
OL,18,Fcommittees.                            
OL,20,FIn Northern Ireland, he said, cuts were
OL,21,F"simply imposed with little or no      
OL,22,Fexplanation".                          
OL,23,EPub: 16-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,143,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14205
SC,0005
PS,C000
CT,5,T
OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 142 Tue 17 NovC16:41/43
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G5/15
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSCStormont backs call for BBC       
OL,4,CNorthern Ireland to explain cuts       
OL,6,FO'Toole was also critical of The Nolan 
OL,7,FShow. He said that on 3rd September,   
OL,8,Fblogger Jamie Bryson was interviewed   
OL,9,Ffor nearly 20 minutes, and the         
OL,10,Fprogramme then went live to a 10am     
OL,11,Fpress conference by Portadown Orange   
OL,12,Flodge in which Mr Bryson took part.    
OL,14,FHe also said DUP MLA Jonathan Buckley  
OL,15,Fhad been given 45 uninterrupted minutes
OL,16,Fon 4th November, followed by TUV leader
OL,17,FJim Allister.                          
OL,19,FHe said these were legitimate stories, 
OL,20,Fbut licence fee payers had a right to  
OL,21,Fask whether they were covered in line  
OL,22,Fwith the BBC's mission.                
OL,23,EPub: 16-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,143,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14206
SC,0006
PS,C000
CT,5,T
OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 142 Tue 17 NovC16:41/43
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G6/15
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSCStormont backs call for BBC       
OL,4,CNorthern Ireland to explain cuts       
OL,6,FIn his closing remarks, he said        
OL,7,F"divisive voices and hard-line actors, 
OL,8,Fbacked by big salaries" were being     
OL,9,F"ring-fenced, protected and promoted"  
OL,10,Fwhile other services were cut.         
OL,12,FSinn Fein's Colm Gildernew, who chairs 
OL,13,Fthe Communities Committee, said the BBC
OL,14,F"has again shown how poorly it         
OL,15,Funderstands this place".               
OL,23,EPub: 16-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,143,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14207
SC,0007
PS,C000
CT,5,T
OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 142 Tue 17 NovC16:41/43
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G7/15
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSCStormont backs call for BBC       
OL,4,CNorthern Ireland to explain cuts       
OL,6,FHe said a promise about the number of  
OL,7,FIrish language hours did not tell      
OL,8,Flisteners whether the programmes they  
OL,9,Fvalued would survive. He called on the 
OL,10,FBBC to reverse the staffing cuts, and  
OL,11,Fsaid he would meet senior BBC staff    
OL,12,Fsoon.                                  
OL,14,FAlliance's Kate Armstrong intervened to
OL,15,Fpoint out that BBC NI dropped sign     
OL,16,Flanguage from its lunchtime news in    
OL,17,FJune 2024. Gildernew agreed, saying    
OL,18,Fthat provision should be restored.     
OL,23,EPub: 16-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,143,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14208
SC,0008
PS,C000
CT,5,T
OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 142 Tue 17 NovC16:41/43
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G8/15
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSCStormont backs call for BBC       
OL,4,CNorthern Ireland to explain cuts       
OL,6,FThe DUP's Deborah Erskine said         
OL,7,Fquestions about efficiency were        
OL,8,Flegitimate, but the BBC must be        
OL,9,Ftransparent about the impact of its    
OL,10,Fsavings.                               
OL,12,FShe warned that "BBC Northern Ireland  
OL,13,Fmust not become 'BBC Belfast'", and    
OL,14,Fsaid Ulster Scots culture must not     
OL,15,Fbecome a casualty of cost-cutting.     
OL,17,FHer party colleague Brian Kingston     
OL,18,Fhighlighted BBC NI successes with a    
OL,19,FUK-wide audience, including Blue Lights
OL,20,Fand Peelers: The PSNI for Real, which  
OL,21,Fbegins on BBC Two this week.           
OL,23,EPub: 16-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,143,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14209
SC,0009
PS,C000
CT,5,T
OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 142 Tue 17 NovC16:41/43
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}         G9/15
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSCStormont backs call for BBC       
OL,4,CNorthern Ireland to explain cuts       
OL,6,FAlliance's Sian Mulholland said she was
OL,7,Fparticularly concerned about the impact
OL,8,Fon the creative workforce, citing      
OL,9,Frepresentations from the Musicians'    
OL,10,FUnion. She called on the BBC to publish
OL,11,Fan explanation of its priorities, and  
OL,12,Fto "pause the cuts".                   
OL,14,FThe UUP's Mike Nesbitt, who worked at  
OL,15,FBBC NI for around a decade and at UTV  
OL,16,Ffor longer, recalled a past round of   
OL,17,FBBC cuts. Every department lost staff, 
OL,18,Fhe said, except personnel, which gained
OL,19,Ftwo extra people to administer the     
OL,20,Fcuts.                                  
OL,23,EPub: 16-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,143,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14210
SC,0010
PS,C000
CT,5,T
OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 142 Tue 17 NovC16:41/43
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}        G10/15
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSCStormont backs call for BBC       
OL,4,CNorthern Ireland to explain cuts       
OL,6,FHe also cited Radio Foyle as a case for
OL,7,Fmore openness. After the morning show  
OL,8,Fwas cut in 2022, Ofcom found the BBC   
OL,9,Fhad breached its licence: it broadcast 
OL,10,F651 hours of news and current affairs  
OL,11,Fon Foyle in 2023/24, against a         
OL,12,Frequirement of 1,043.                  
OL,14,FThe BBC blamed an "internal            
OL,15,Fmiscommunication".                     
OL,17,FNesbitt said UTV had always been seen  
OL,18,Flocally as "a truly local station". By 
OL,19,Fcontrast, he said, the BBC's use of    
OL,20,FLondon presenters during the Troubles  
OL,21,Fmade it look like "a branch office".   
OL,23,EPub: 16-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,143,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14211
SC,0011
PS,C000
CT,5,T
OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 142 Tue 17 NovC16:41/43
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}        G11/15
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSCStormont backs call for BBC       
OL,4,CNorthern Ireland to explain cuts       
OL,6,FSinn Fein's Nicola Brogan accused the  
OL,7,FBBC of institutional bias against Irish
OL,8,Fnationalism, though she said this had  
OL,9,Fimproved. She contrasted the 60% cut to
OL,10,FIrish language staff with a cut of     
OL,11,Faround 10% across the wider            
OL,12,Forganisation.                          
OL,14,FThe SDLP's Patsy McGlone, speaking in  
OL,15,FIrish, said Irish speakers in Northern 
OL,16,FIreland have about 30 minutes a day on 
OL,17,FRadio Ulster and Radio Foyle, far less 
OL,18,Fthan Welsh and Gaelic speakers get. He 
OL,19,Fasked whether an outsourced model could
OL,20,Fserve a growing language community.    
OL,23,EPub: 16-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,143,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14212
SC,0012
PS,C000
CT,5,T
OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 142 Tue 17 NovC16:41/43
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}        G12/15
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSCStormont backs call for BBC       
OL,4,CNorthern Ireland to explain cuts       
OL,6,FThe only dissenting voice came from the
OL,7,FTUV's Timothy Gaston. He said the BBC  
OL,8,F"should be defunded for its continued  
OL,9,Fbias".                                 
OL,11,FHe cited a 2025 report linking a Comber
OL,12,FOrange lodge statement to a cancelled  
OL,13,Fchildren's GAA and cricket camp, which 
OL,14,Fhe said the BBC took nine months to    
OL,15,Fcorrect.                               
OL,23,EPub: 16-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,143,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14213
SC,0013
PS,C000
CT,5,T
OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 142 Tue 17 NovC16:41/43
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}        G13/15
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSCStormont backs call for BBC       
OL,4,CNorthern Ireland to explain cuts       
OL,6,FPeople Before Profit's Gerry Carroll   
OL,7,Fsaid bias "works the other way", but   
OL,8,Fargued the licence fee was unfair and  
OL,9,Fshould be linked to income. He also    
OL,10,Fwarned that moving production to the   
OL,11,Findependent sector often meant lower   
OL,12,Fpay and fewer rights for workers.      
OL,14,FClosing the debate, O'Toole said the   
OL,15,Fclosure of BBC NI's entire in-house    
OL,16,Ffactual unit was, as far as he knew,   
OL,17,Fnot happening in Scotland or Wales.    
OL,19,FHe said MLAs could not be asked to     
OL,20,Faccept a "broad-based slashing of      
OL,21,Fservices" just because shows such as   
OL,22,FBlue Lights succeed.                   
OL,23,EPub: 16-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
FL,143,140,200,120,0,100
PN,14214
SC,0014
PS,C000
CT,5,T
OL,0,       GCEEFAX 1 142 Tue 17 NovC16:41/43
OL,1,W~+$ hw1~{4~k4 ~shw1~sj7}        G14/15
OL,2,W+.!+,"-$/*%/*% / "-$+,*-'U(,,,,,,,,,,,,
OL,3,GNEWSCStormont backs call for BBC       
OL,4,CNorthern Ireland to explain cuts       
OL,6,FResponding to the debate, a BBC        
OL,7,Fspokesperson said the corporation seeks
OL,8,Fto reflect a breadth of views and does 
OL,9,Fnot give anyone "uncritical access to  
OL,10,Fthe BBC's airwaves".                   
OL,12,FThe spokesperson said the BBC's aim    
OL,13,F"will be to protect the quality and    
OL,14,Fdistinctiveness of what we do".        
OL,16,FThe BBC has previously said its        
OL,17,Fspending on Irish language content, and
OL,18,Foutput on Radio Ulster and Radio Foyle,
OL,19,Fwill not change.                       
OL,23,EPub: 16-Nov-2026Upppppppppppppppppppppp
OL,24,ANext PageBClean FeedCNat TVFOn This Day
